<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The graph of <m>y = {2\sin 2x}</m> is mapped onto <m>y = {2\sin(2x + 100^\circ) + 1}</m> by a translation. Give the translation vector.</p><div><tabular style="display:inline-table;vertical-align:middle;border-collapse:collapse;"><row><cell rowspan="2" style="font-size:3em;padding:0 4px;">(</cell><cell style="padding:2px;"><fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/> <m>^\circ</m></cell><cell rowspan="2" style="font-size:3em;padding:0 4px;">)</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:2px;"><fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/></cell></row></tabular></div><div>   </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Take out the <m>{2}</m>: <m>y = {2\sin 2(x + 50^\circ) + 1}</m>.</p><p>Replacing <m>x</m> by <m>x { + 50}^\circ</m> moves the graph the opposite way to the sign, by the angle divided by <m>{2}</m>: <m>{50}^\circ</m> to the left. Adding <m>{1}</m> outside moves every point up by <m>{1}</m>.</p><p>The translation vector is <m>\begin{pmatrix} {-50}^\circ \\ {1} \end{pmatrix}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>-50</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>